  "published": "2026-11-10T20:56:46.03Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n- The packages no longer have a `net8.0` build. An application on .NET 8 or .NET 9 gets a .NET Standard build, without the APIs that only the `net10.0` build has, such as `DateOnly` and `TimeOnly` support. To keep those APIs, move the application to .NET 10.\n- The `netstandard1.x` and `netstandard2.0` builds no longer list `JetBrains.Annotations` as a NuGet dependency. If your code uses its attributes and you got the package through DataStandardizer, add a reference to `JetBrains.Annotations` to your project.\n\nFixed:\n- Debuggers can step into the packages' source through Source Link.\n- Iso3166Part2Subdivision.CompareTo orders subdivisions by code instead of throwing.\n- Iso3166Part2Subdivision.CompareTo(null) returns a positive value instead of throwing ArgumentNullException.\n- `GetSubdivisionNativeName` and `GetSubdivisionNativeNameLocalVariant` without a romanization system return the name ISO 3166-2 lists first for the language, by a documented rule instead of attribute enumeration order.\n- UnM49Extensions.GetM49Codes throws ArgumentException, not InvalidCastException, for an enum that isn't a UN M49 enumeration.\n- `Iso3166Extensions.GetSubdivisionParentCode` carries `[return: MaybeNull]` on the .NET Standard builds, so a caller with nullable reference types enabled is warned before dereferencing its result, as on .NET 10.\n- The UN M49 name lookups match the language code without regard to case, as the ISO 3166 lookups do.\n\nChanged:\n- The netstandard1.x and netstandard2.0 builds now carry nullable annotations, so projects on C# 8 or later with nullable enabled get null warnings from them.\n- `UnM49Extensions.GetM49Codes` and `GetM49Codes<T>` throw `ArgumentException` for an enum that has no members, or a member without `UnM49AreaCodeAttribute`.",
